{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DCJJ","id":"629235245291667476","is_bot":0,"username":"dcjj"},"author_id":"629235245291667476","channel_id":"739055666651463691","content":"```Dear Wynne, the hunger soon approaches. We have had small victories setting up defenses for us in #hex-z-the-hanging-tree, however now we need to set up some offensive tactics for us. I have a few ideas that can help; but i need assistance in them. As well as your approval. Please look over these ideas, and let me know any changes or additions you feel should be made. Thank you:\n\nTo any spell casters: If you can use the spell “Glyph” I ask that you set up as many as possible can in the area. All necessary gold will be provided if necessary to pay for the supplies to do this. Set the trigger to what you feel is most appropriate.\nTo our long range fighters, I ask that you prepare your weapons to be more consistent and damaging. Whether they would be needing oil to make flaming arrows, or any thing else you can think of. If supplies are needed they will be provided.\nTo our Jackalopes, I ask that you use your natural abilities of burrowing to set up tunnels under the coming battle field. This would allow our allies to move about and prepare an ambush to attack from all sides. If possible, also set it up for them to be blocked off or destroyed if they are used against us. \nTo our aerial citizens, I ask you prepare items or weapons that can be dropped on our enemies from a good height. We will use the force of gravity as our ally to  slow there advance and allow our long range fighters to pick them off.\n\nThese are unfortunately all I have thought of so far. Any ideas or suggestions you have are greatly appreciated.\n\nThank you for reading,\nYour friend, Copper.```","created_at":"2020-08-18T18:41:00.963000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"745351564600016996","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
